@bank all
// PLACEHOLDERS (the career engineer, 0.61.0): head writer 4 writes the real ones. Leave, missed shifts and being let
// go (design-doc "Leave, missed shifts and being let go"). worried.*: a friend (colleague or closer) comes and finds you
// after each step down. farewell.*: friends' goodbyes when you've been let go. The career.* kinds are read as plain
// text, not spoken (no voice tokens; {me} is fine): tips, Mail ("subject | body") and the closing card ("title | body").

== worried.chief
- Calder had you in the office, didn't she? You all right, {nick}?
- Heard you had a word with the Chief. If something's wrong, tell me.

== worried.captain
- The Captain sent for you. That's serious, {nick}. What's going on?
- People are talking about the ready room. I'm worried about you.

== worried.last
- They'll send you home if this goes on. Please turn up tomorrow.
- One good shift, {nick}. That's all it takes to start. Please.

== farewell.eve
- I heard. Tomorrow? I can't believe it. I'm going to miss you, {me}.
- It's not fair. Well, it is. But I'll miss you anyway.

== farewell.day
- Write to me, {me}. Every week. Promise.   #warm
- The Wren won't be the same. Look after yourself out there.   #warm

== career.tip.leave
- Leave: book a workday off here, by 07:30 on the day. You start with 3 days and earn 1 more every four weeks, up to 5.
== career.tip.late
- You were late for your shift. A small dip in how Works sees you. Be in the Works bay by 08:00.
== career.tip.missed
- You missed your shift with no leave booked. That's a big hit to your work standing. Need a day? Book leave on your device.
== career.tip.chief
- The Chief has sent for you: your work standing is low. Go to the meeting, then turn up for shifts and do jobs to recover.
== career.tip.captain
- The Captain has sent for you. Your standing is very low: one step from being sent home. Every shift you work helps.
== career.tip.bottom
- Your work standing is at the bottom. Three days like this and you'll be let go. One good shift turns it round.
== career.tip.notice
- You've been let go. Tomorrow is your last day on the Wren. Your friends will want to say goodbye.
== career.mail.chief
- My office | Come to my office on Deck 5 at the time on your device. We need to talk about your shifts. Calder
== career.mail.captain
- The Captain wants to see you | The Captain will see you in her ready room on Deck 1 at the time on your device. Be there.
== career.mail.notice
- Your posting | I'm sorry it's come to this. You're being sent home. Your shuttle leaves tomorrow at 15:00. Calder
== career.card
- Your time on the Wren is over | The shuttle pulls away. The Wren grows small behind you. Someone else opens the Works bay at 08:00.
